		<div class="topic" id="forum_op_topic_572679490124411134">
		Feature request: AI to player narrative control	</div>
	<div class="content" id="forum_op_content_572679490124411134">
		Could we have a button next to the god mode button to toggle on a passive mode where if the NPC/AI is about to prompt an interaction directly with the player while narrative control mode is active it pauses the game with a menu showing what they are about to do.<br>I would have an input box for the player to direct or instruct the outcome of the interaction so the AI doesn't automatically assume the outcome of an interaction and then you have to correct it somehow with OOC or with a following interaction. But if the player doesn't put anything into the input box then the game behaves like normal and the AI would just assume the interaction outcome like it normally does if the player wants to leave the mode on but doesn't want to direct the AI each time.	</div>
		
	<div class="forum_op_footer">
		<div class="forum_audit">
			Last edited by <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/id/GproKaru" class="hoverunderline">GproKaru</a>;
		<span  title="November 3, 2026 @ 3:52:00 am PST" data-timestamp="1793706720">22 hours ago</span>		</div>
			</div>
</div>
